        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T17:09:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So we don\u0027t run configure at all on non-tests if given --test but not --build?\n\nThis seems like an odd and unexpected behavior.\n\nWhat\u0027s the use case, and if it\u0027s required, can we make it a switch, like --tests-only? Or a more general idea would be \"--filter\u003dproject.config.is_test\" to allow filtering to certain projects?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 252,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 257,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f2b6b61d24741e674146a0bd91eeadc4e3c0d163",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57ac324f_5909aee2",
        "filename": "zephyr/zmake/zmake/zmake.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 257,
      "author": {
        "id": 1483403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T18:20:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Look at the table in the bug. In gitlab and also in the CQ, I really want a \"build\" step that builds all the boards, and a \"test\" step that only runs the tests.  And this is what `zmake coverage` does today.\n\nI\u0027d be fine with having `zmake configureall --build` build all boards and tests, and then `zmake testall` that runs the tests, but doesn\u0027t build anything.\n\nBut this discussion probably should be in the bug, as there you can see the implications of changing any particular logic.",
      "parentUuid": "173270bf_16f5b516",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 252,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 257,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "f2b6b61d24741e674146a0bd91eeadc4e3c0d163",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c8e85f8_2b80ec96",
